/typing/typing_edit.py`, since the spec doesn't list it as a command.\n\n- **`src/click/termui.py`**:\n  - I added `import os` and the new `filename` annotation on both overloads and the implementation.\n  - The body now wraps a single `str` or `os.PathLike` in a one-item tuple.\n  - The docstring has the new \"It accepts a path or any iterable of paths.\" sentence and the `versionchanged:: 8.5.0` entry.\n- **`src/click/_termui_impl.py`**: `Editor.edit_files` takes the new type. The spec said to change the body only if needed. I did change it, converting each item with `os.fspath` when building the command. I did this so every entry reaches the editor process as a plain string.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: the spec says to add the entry to the `Unreleased` list. The file has no `Unreleased` heading; the top section is `Version 8.5.0`, with no release date. I appended the entry at the end of that section.", "ttft_ms": 1965, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 27148, "uuid": "86f44f94-2167-4cac-843f-791b054f4b70", "ttft_stream_ms": 1614, "time_to_request_ms": 50, "first_content_frame_ms": 1614, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
